Subject: Competitive play: a set that lost its connection leaves the online menus
Upstream-base: a353c8f2dfb34eb08fecd725965a46ea629428e3

A set's game whose connection to the opponent's broke (the game's popup
ended the set) came back to the online menu and stayed online in WFC, where
the next set or the player's RANKED could meet a stranger. SHOnlineHub::Update
now asks the module (src/platform/competitive_match.cpp) once the menu is
ready, and leaves for the main menu as the menu's Back does.

diff --git a/include/mscharged_competitive.h b/include/mscharged_competitive.h
--- a/include/mscharged_competitive.h
+++ b/include/mscharged_competitive.h
@@ -84,6 +84,13 @@
 #endif
 
 #if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+// The online menu, ready: a set whose game lost its connection to the
+// opponent's (or that was called off) is over, and the game leaves the
+// online menus for the main menu as the menu's Back does (tweak patch 0055).
+bool mscharged_competitive_leave_online(void);
+#endif
+
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
 // The set's players by their profile names (tweak patch 0050): the game shows
